    {
      "name": "Cash plan",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "name": "Plan summary",
          "source": "# Payday cash plan\n\nUse the editable **As of** date and opening cash to plan known deposits and bills. Amounts are signed: income is positive and spending is negative. The two projected balances use the same calendar with a baseline and a lean grocery and discretionary scenario.\n\n{% let reserve = Assumptions!B2 %}\n{% let baselineLow = MIN(CashEvents[BaselineBalance]) %}\n{% let leanLow = MIN(CashEvents[LeanBalance]) %}\n**Baseline low:** {{ TEXT(baselineLow, \"$#,##0.00\") }} on {{ TEXT(INDEX(CashEvents[Date], MATCH(baselineLow, CashEvents[BaselineBalance], 0)), \"mmm d\") }}. **Lean low:** {{ TEXT(leanLow, \"$#,##0.00\") }}. The reserve target is {{ TEXT(reserve, \"$#,##0.00\") }}.\n\nThe brake repair brings the baseline below the reserve target. Try changing the October 14 **LeanAmount** from -170 to -140; the lean low should rise by $30 and clear the target. Update the opening cash and event estimates when your real dates or balances change."
        },
        {
